  "text": "Inauguration stones are a Celtic sacred object. Kings commonly took office while standing on a sacred stone. The best known was the Lia Fáil. Legend held that it came from the Otherworld to stand on the hill of Tara. Some myths say the true stone stayed in the Otherworld and a copy came to the world. The Lia Fáil was to scream when the true king touched it. According to one legend the original, also called the Stone of Destiny, moved to Scotland. There it crowned 34 kings. In 1296 Edward I carried it to Westminster Abbey. It witnessed the crowning of every British monarch but Mary I. In 1996 it returned to Scotland.",
